ommunication barriers"}]}, {"id": "2f6bdd18-f36b-4e61-8bc9-683792a93003", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sensitive and trauma-informed history", "description": "Students learn to ask difficult questions safely and respectfully.", "children": [{"id": "20d6bf15-03d5-4b08-b777-683d9eff9fc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Sexual, substance use, mental health, violence, and safety history"}, {"id": "9c12623e-b95a-4dd3-907c-c81de1d0004a", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma-informed choice, control, and pacing"}, {"id": "8a17d503-e171-4ee0-b20b-a33128d6ebb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality and mandated reporting boundaries"}]}]}, {"id": "26a88d2a-21b3-46d9-9191-94d5a84fc552", "type": "topic", "title": "General survey, vital signs, pain, and clinical measurement", "description": "Recognize baseline appearance, distress, vital sign patterns, pain, and early warning changes.", "children": [{"id": "36477c01-7053-43f4-aa95-eb83bac0d7a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "General survey", "description": "Students learn to form a first clinical impression from appearance, behavior, mobility, and distress.", "children": [{"id": "8aac32fa-0e2a-4f18-bdd0-aea1a3e13539", "type": "concept", "title": "Level of consciousness and orientation"}, {"id": "c832d65b-d4b7-40a6-bce5-77cb45ba5e5b", "type": "concept", "title": "Body habitus, posture, hygiene, and affect"}, {"id": "25e31aca-2e97-48a7-a950-b366196766d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Signs of acute distress and immediate risk"}]}, {"id": "64c773f3-1af2-412f-abe4-036ccc642066", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Vital signs and measurement accuracy", "description": "This subtopic teaches how technique affects interpretation and escalation.", "children": [{"id": "b41d993e-de91-4b4e-b5d9-07e5eeeb4c37", "type": "concept", "title": "Temperature, pulse, respirations, blood pressure, SpO2"}, {"id": "01bd666d-3b2c-4ba7-b766-f2fa70676886", "type": "concept", "title": "Orthostatic vital signs and pain as an assessment domain"}, {"id": "65fdd777-e421-4022-984c-66132026d864", "type": "concept", "title": "Equipment sizing, positioning, and repeat measurement"}]}, {"id": "d2e21c13-d735-4d27-92b5-43fa075ec50c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Early warning and escalation", "description": "Students learn when assessment findings require urgent reassessment or notification.", "children": [{"id": "4e205aa8-dbfd-4384-b67c-cfe152a506a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Trend recognition"}, {"id": "ccb5d3fc-de8f-4733-8b4f-0dc59f155be1", "type": "concept", "title": "Red flags and abnormal ranges"}, {"id": "b3f58dc4-abde-45e5-8bca-1ba997fa2f6a", "type": "concept", "title": "SBAR-style communication"}]}]}, {"id": "1a48a91c-1229-46a6-85d8-7aa53f89aa0f", "type": "topic", "title": "Skin, hair, nails, lymphatics, and pressure-injury risk", "description": "Assess the integumentary system for normal variation, lesions, perfusion, infection, wounds, and risk.", "children": [{"id": "a0dc6168-be72-4bda-af23-cb86854cd43e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inspection and palpation of skin", "description": "Students learn to identify normal variation, lesions, perfusion changes, and infection clues.", "children": [{"id": "1bca077c-7387-4a00-8431-855b30458b2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Color, temperature, moisture, turgor, texture"}, {"id": "a15892dd-07b8-4b00-b053-8d5cff8c749a", "type": "concept", "title": "Lesion description and distribution"}, {"id": "857064c5-17a7-4a7b-bdd0-ae64dfa8c5ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Cyanosis, pallor, jaundice, erythema, and bruising"}]}, {"id": "e7a16116-354d-424a-88ac-5ff45f567535", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Wounds and pressure injury risk", "description": "This subtopic teaches structured risk recognition and documentation.", "children": [{"id": "01c53d63-3404-47d8-aaf8-b84c8cfea245", "type": "concept", "title": "Pressure injury staging concepts"}, {"id": "2f225c88-8776-42ed-ba9e-c029bbbd6bac", "type": "concept", "title": "Wound size, drainage, odor, and surrounding skin"}, {"id": "88bb