ight change, intake, appetite, swallowing, and food access"}, {"id": "368f0acb-6310-4035-b21d-b89aad7fcc34", "type": "concept", "title": "Hydration, mucous membranes, edema, and output"}, {"id": "4914681b-8209-48f8-97f4-1d3fa0eb4f8d", "type": "concept", "title": "Bowel patterns, constipation, diarrhea, and ostomies"}]}, {"id": "3f3cef26-ece0-4b1e-a697-f207477fdd2f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Genitourinary and reproductive assessment", "description": "Students learn dignity-preserving ways to assess sensitive symptoms and risks.", "children": [{"id": "0c299845-f771-4a3a-a9a4-95c2898297a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Urinary symptoms, continence, and catheter assessment"}, {"id": "5e41efa2-2a19-43cc-8eac-2767924f32a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Menstrual, sexual, and reproductive health history"}, {"id": "469da36e-f1f3-48a6-ae09-f23b6ce73f8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy, consent, chaperones, and referral boundaries"}]}]}, {"id": "d8482ba8-7a94-460d-91c7-8c365e95969c", "type": "topic", "title": "Musculoskeletal, functional, mobility, and falls assessment", "description": "Assess strength, range of motion, gait, function, safety, and mobility risk.", "children": [{"id": "12518c61-6206-4583-9545-b38a0d8cef1b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Musculoskeletal exam", "description": "Students learn to assess structure, motion, strength, and pain.", "children": [{"id": "baba6a7e-f1e5-486d-be4a-02cb5e4e80d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Inspection, symmetry, swelling, deformity"}, {"id": "9494f61b-f3fc-4e01-aa13-d89690e326e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Range of motion and strength grading concepts"}, {"id": "f52fb959-009d-460b-bf8c-8105a122c256", "type": "concept", "title": "Joint pain, back pain, and functional impact"}]}, {"id": "31a13128-eaf6-49fd-a45b-2545a9570fb6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Functional assessment", "description": "This subtopic connects body-system findings to the patient's ability to live safely.", "children": [{"id": "c491cda4-f2