ssessment", "description": "This subtopic expands assessment beyond body systems to lived context.", "children": [{"id": "167cf208-df1f-4a1f-8255-9e6ec58a2abe", "type": "concept", "title": "Culture, spirituality, family structure, and identity"}, {"id": "4aead30c-e23d-4fdf-83cb-abb73eeeb440", "type": "concept", "title": "Social determinants of health"}, {"id": "a0c406b7-6b0c-47aa-9afb-571f8a66a1df", "type": "concept", "title": "Health literacy, language, and trust"}]}, {"id": "2dd55b6d-c5d5-445c-833a-0d654ccf3683", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accessibility and trauma-informed care", "description": "Students learn to make assessment safer and more accurate for people with disability, trauma history, or communication needs.", "children": [{"id": "65aae9df-e9e3-4591-b03b-46f36a3b0efb", "type": "concept", "title": "Mobility, sensory, cognitive, and communication accommodations"}, {"id": "2e16996a-46b7-4141-bb31-8253773b0e44", "type": "concept", "title": "Choice, control, collaboration, and empowerment"}, {"id": "f8640b1a-4cdf-4ecf-8a93-bd980c0d8f1c", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding retraumatization and preserving dignity"}]}]}, {"id": "64b01260-feee-4ce8-9066-9d4e592d2339", "type": "topic", "title": "Clinical reasoning, documentation, diagnostic stewardship, and simulation integration", "description": "Turn assessment findings into priorities, documentation, escalation, screening choices, and OSCE-ready practice.", "children": [{"id": "84df1299-7223-4220-9d01-a7f24517faa5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Clinical reasoning from assessment data", "description": "Students learn to cluster cues, identify concerns, and decide what to do next.", "children": [{"id": "6ba2fc8c-757a-4e52-8153-c33f61d5215d", "type": "concept", "title": "Normal versus abnormal findings"}, {"id": "2995dce8-5af7-4870-9048-42e4b6b6ecb4", "type": "concept", "title": "Cue recognition and hypothesis generation"}, {"id": "5f2315fd-ce86-4796-93f6-d548a66722ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Prioritization, reassessment, and escalation"}]}, {"id": "59e8f014-1162-4cb5-ab94-978136b4e149", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Documentation and handoff", "description": "This subtopic turns observations into clear, defensible clinical communication.", "children": [{"id": "fc7cb43d-e45f-4dcb-b507-809a86c7454b", "type": "concept", "title": "Objective description and approved terminology"}, {"id": "eec90ac6-9b96-4c92-9ee2-2af9df14230d", "type": "concept", "title": "Focused notes, flowsheets, and EHR considerations"}, {"id": "5819fdff-6e74-4467-9f1c-e14145d90a48", "type": "concept", "title": "SBAR, change-in-condition reporting, and follow-up plans"}]}, {"id": "29e8d58a-9f62-49f0-a567-8f600f8b37c4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diagnostic stewardship and simulation", "description": "Students learn to use tests and simulations thoughtfully, avoiding both missed diagnoses and unnecessary testing.", "children": [{"id": "11db227d-a0a4-449e-b6ab-5f80fc8ef5f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Screening guidelines and test selection"}, {"id": "efeacaf2-fb9e-4801-b683-328a0fd61dc5", "type": "concept", "title": "Diagnostic safety, uncertainty, and follow-up"}, {"id": "033598f6-bda9-4895-9363-b9e14f4c4346", "type": "concept", "title": "OSCE practice, checklists, and reflective improvement"}]}]}], "dbBacked": true}$hajson$::jsonb,
